  "scope": "The production application's Fury, Arms, Protection and Fury Protection Warrior and Elemental and Enhancement Shaman reference builds against 2, 3, 4 and 5 copies of the boss, each built by the application's own BuildRequest with its Advanced targets setting and AoE lines (application revision 3923f70de), and 29 variants of them that cast what the lines leave out (Thunder Clap, Chain Lightning with Magma Totem, multidot lines for Rend and Flame Shock), cast Cleave first, drop Cleave or Weaponmaster, or stand in front of the boss, exported with the pinned Go engine and run by Go and Rust.",
  "generator": "tools/reference-capture/builds/main.go in a scratch module that requires the application's worker: builds -targets N <scratch> warrior arms-warrior protection-warrior fury-protection-warrior elemental-shaman enhancement-shaman, for N from 2 to 5. The variants edit those requests' priority lists. arms-warrior-clap inserts a Thunder Clap (11581) cast at the fourth place when numberTargets is at least 2; arms-warrior-clap-nowm also sets the Arms tree's Weaponmaster rank (the 14th digit of the talents string) to 0; arms-warrior-clap-no-cleave removes the Cleave (20569) lines from arms-warrior-clap at 4 and 5 targets; warrior-cleave-first puts a Cleave cast first when numberTargets is at least 2 and rage is at least 20; warrior-whirlwind removes the Cleave lines from warrior at 4 and 5 targets; enhancement-shaman-chain-magma inserts a Magma Totem (10587) cast when numberTargets is at least 2 and the fire totem has expired, then a Chain Lightning (10605) cast when numberTargets is at least 2, after the first priority line; arms-warrior-multidot-rend inserts a multidot line for Rend (11574, 5 dots, no overlap) after the Rend line, and elemental-shaman-multidot-flame-shock one for Flame Shock (29228) after its line, at 3 and 5 targets; the -front variants (arms-warrior-front at 3 targets, warrior-front, arms-warrior-clap-front, enhancement-shaman-front at 5, 5 and 3) set the player's inFrontOfTarget; arms-warrior-clap-1-target takes the one target Arms reference build, makes its Sweeping Strikes cast unconditional and inserts the Thunder Clap line",
  "rerun": "python3 tools/prepared_v2.py compare --output <scratch> validation/2026-10-06-multi-target-warrior-shaman-references/*.json",
